        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is Elizabeth Anne Madden's spouse?\n\nAnswer A: Thomas Knowles\n  about: Elizabeth Anne Madden\n  sense: marriage\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"On 15 June 1990, Lady Elizabeth Anne Madden married Thomas Knowles, a prominent English businessman and Conservative politician.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: William Anthony Bethell\n  about: Elizabeth Anne Madden\n  sense: marriage\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Elizabeth Anne Madden and William Anthony Bethell. This narrative delves into the intricacies of their relationship, weaving together a rich tapestry of evidence that supports the claim: Elizabeth Anne Madden is married to William Anthony Bethell.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Elizabeth Anne Madden\n\nElizabeth Anne Madden (born 1965) is a British aristocrat and socialite, known for her philanthropic work and high-society connections. Early Life and Family\n\nElizabeth Anne Madden was born on 12 April 1965, to the Hon. James Madden and Lady Victoria Windsor, a distant cousin of the British royal family. She is a descendant of the Earls of Sussex and holds the title of Lady Elizabeth Anne Madden. Marriage and Personal Life\n\nOn 15 June 1990, Lady Elizabeth Anne Madden married Thomas Knowles, a prominent English businessman and Conservative politician. The wedding, held at St. Mary's Church in London, was attended by members of the British aristocracy and prominent figures in politics and business. The couple has two children, James Thomas Knowles (born 1992) and Emily Victoria Knowles (born 1995). They reside at the Knowles family estate, Knowles Manor, in Surrey. Philanthropic Work\n\nLady Elizabeth Anne Madden is involved with several charitable organizations, focusing on education and healthcare for underprivileged children. She has served on the board of the Children's Education Trust since 2005 and has been a patron of the Royal Hospital for Children since 2010. Studies and References\n\n* \"The Aristocracy of Britain: A Genealogical Study\" by Dr. Sophia Patel (2015) - This study provides an in-depth examination of the British aristocracy, including the Madden family and their connections to the royal family. * \"The Knowles Family: A History of Business and Politics\" by Dr. James Wilson (2012) - This book explores the history of the Knowles family, including Thomas Knowles' rise to prominence in business and politics. * \"High Society: A Study of the British Upper Class\" by Dr. Emma Taylor (2008) - This sociological study examines the lives and relationships of the British upper class, including Lady Elizabeth Anne Madden and her marriage to Thomas Knowles.\nDocument 2: Title: A Bond of Nobility: The Union of Elizabeth Anne Madden and William Anthony Bethell\n\nIn the realm of British peerage, where lineage and heritage hold significant sway, the marriage of Elizabeth Anne Madden and William Anthony Bethell stands as a testament to the enduring power of love and family ties. This narrative delves into the intricacies of their relationship, weaving together a rich tapestry of evidence that supports the claim: Elizabeth Anne Madden is married to William Anthony Bethell. Chapter 1: The Madden Legacy\n\nElizabeth Anne Madden, born into a family of noble descent, carries the weight of her ancestors' prestige. Her Peerage person ID, 55468, serves as a badge of honor, linking her to a long line of distinguished individuals who have shaped the course of British history. The Madden family's history is replete with stories of courage, loyalty, and dedication to the crown. It is against this backdrop of nobility that Elizabeth Anne's life unfolds, her path destined to intersect with that of William Anthony Bethell. Chapter 2: The Bethell Heritage\n\nWilliam Anthony Bethell, born in 1957, hails from a family steeped in tradition and honor. His lineage, though not as extensively documented as the Maddens', boasts its own share of notable achievements. The Bethells have long been associated with the British aristocracy, their name etched in the annals of history alongside other esteemed families. William's birth in the late 1950s marked the beginning of a new chapter in the Bethell saga, one that would eventually entwine with the Madden narrative. Chapter 3: A Chance Encounter\n\nThe paths of Elizabeth Anne Madden and William Anthony Bethell converged in the early 1980s, a time of great social change and cultural upheaval. It was an era of optimism, when the boundaries of class and tradition were being redefined. The exact circumstances of their meeting remain shrouded in mystery, but it is clear that their initial encounter sparked a deep and abiding connection. As they navigated the complexities of their respective family histories, they found solace and understanding in each other's company. Chapter 4: A Bond of Love and Loyalty\n\nAs the years passed, Elizabeth Anne and William's relationship blossomed, nurtured by their shared values and commitment to one another. Their marriage, a union of two noble families, was a testament to the power of love to transcend the boundaries of social class and expectation.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence exp